"""
NVMe controller INITIALISATION, end to end, over the host-equivalent path.

The sequence a real host performs, in order:
  read CAP -> write AQA/ASQ/ACQ -> set CC.EN -> wait for CSTS.RDY
  -> Identify over the admin queue -> create an I/O queue pair
  -> PRP-backed write and read.

SCOPE, STATED PLAINLY: the stages are exercised by THREE in-tree programs,
not one. Each block below runs one program and asserts its stage tokens.
This proves every stage of the sequence is exercised; it does NOT prove a
single uninterrupted host session walks all of them.

MUST RUN FROM THE REPO ROOT. fw/nvme_transport_config.spl holds a
cwd-relative SDN path; from anywhere else the transport profile silently
reads as zeroes and the run produces plausible-looking false failures.

CLAIM BOUNDARY. This file does not prove NVMe conformance. It proves that
the named in-tree programs ran and printed the named lines, on a host-model
Simple run. It does not prove a linked firmware image, a QEMU or board
execution, PCIe interoperability, or byte-accurate structure layouts.
"""

